{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01EsCYF1Gxr59yDziFwXBQmf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Anchor** is a single-user personal productivity and R&D mission-control system for J.C. Liechty, living entirely in `C:\\dev\\Anchor` (no syncing, no siblings). Grounded claims:\n\n- **It's a local web app + CLI over plain markdown.** `anchor_gui.py` is a self-contained Python-stdlib HTTP server (binds `http://localhost:8777`, run persistently as the NSSM Windows service `anchor`) that generates the full dashboard HTML on each request and reads/writes markdown files directly. `anchor.py` mirrors the same logic as a CLI and regenerates a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **Markdown is the source of truth â€” no database.** Tasks, projects, inbox, and archives are plain `.md` files (`DASHBOARD.md`, `PROJECTS.md`, `INBOX.md`, `domains/*.md`, `CANCELLED.md`, `SAVED_FOR_LATER.md`). It manages a task lifecycle: Active â†’ Done/Cancelled/Saved â†’ Restored, with capture, add, edit, and priority operations.\n\n- **Core productivity surface:** a daily dashboard (focus items, priorities, deadlines, inbox count), per-domain views (academic, commercial, family, writing), quick capture, and a self-test `anchor_healthcheck.py` that runs at 5 AM via Task Scheduler and writes daily reports.\n\n- **It ships an \"R&D Control Surface\" that turns each project into a cockpit for the trio workflow** (researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman). Across four versioned iterations (v2 sessions/summaries/grass; v3 \"Mission Control\" ConPTY terminals + git-worktree isolation + window manager + GWL branding; v4 \"Project Cockpit\" â€” the current built+merged state as of 2026-06-13). It provides: a per-project Kanban/lane view, real interactive terminals (ConPTY via the one permitted native dep `pywinpty`), cached/validated AI session & project summaries, per-session worktree isolation, deliverable pin/declare/launch-by-type, an engine toggle (Claudeâ†”Gemini), a grass-catchers idea board, and cost/tokens/time rollups.\n\n- **Strict constraints by design:** Python stdlib only (sole exception: optional `pywinpty` for terminals, which degrades gracefully); everything stays human-readable and accessible from any CLI/editor; `distro.py` enforces the no-extra-dependencies rule.\n\nIn short: **a markdown-backed personal task/project manager that has grown a sophisticated, terminal-driven control surface for running and tracking AI \"trio\" R&D work on the user's own projects.**"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":4412,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":45292,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"264da72a-3a22-42a0-91c4-29c831b2a5b8","uuid":"ed10769b-86d3-4117-84df-8b22763b840d","request_id":"req_011Cc1HjGWQLKxJwZ282sVLL"}
